## Overview

This document defines the **only correct way** to implement dialog forms in the Cyréna solution after the MudBlazor migration. All dialog forms — create, edit, and confirmation — must follow this pattern exactly.

The pattern is established by three canonical implementations:
- `OllamaConnectionForm` / `OllamaSettings` in **Cyrena.Runtime.Ollama**
- `OpenAIConnectionForm` / `OpenAISettings` in **Cyrena.Runtime.OpenAI**
- `ServerForm` / `Servers` in **Cyrena.Extensa.Components**

---

## Architecture

A dialog form involves **two components**:

1. **The Dialog Form Component** — the content that appears inside the dialog (e.g. `OllamaConnectionForm`)
2. **The Caller Component** — the page or component that opens the dialog (e.g. `OllamaSettings`)

The dialog is **not** shown via local boolean state (`@bind-Visible`). It is shown via `IDialogService.ShowAsync<T>()` and closed via the cascading `IMudDialogInstance`.

---

## 1. The Dialog Form Component

### Razor File Structure

```razor
<MudDialog>
    <DialogContent>
        <MudForm @ref="_form" Model="Model">
            <MudTextField @bind-Value="Model.SomeProperty" Label="Some Property" Required="true" />
            <!-- additional fields -->
        </MudForm>
    </DialogContent>
    <DialogActions>
        <MudButton OnClick="Cancel" Color="Color.Error">Cancel</MudButton>
        <MudButton OnClick="Submit">Submit</MudButton>
    </DialogActions>
</MudDialog>
```

**Rules:**
- `<MudDialog>` has **no** `@bind-Visible` or `@bind-IsVisible` attribute
- Uses `<DialogContent>` and `<DialogActions>` named render fragments
- Contains a `<MudForm @ref="_form" Model="Model">` for validation
- Action buttons call methods on the code-behind

### Code-Behind (`*.razor.cs`)

```csharp
public partial class MyDialogForm
{
    [Parameter] 
    public MyModel Model { get; set; } = default!;

    [CascadingParameter]
    private IMudDialogInstance MudDialog { get; set; } = default!;

    private MudForm _form = default!;

    private async Task Submit()
    {       
        await _form.ValidateAsync();
        if (_form.IsValid)
            MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Ok(Model));
    }

    private void Cancel()
    {
        MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Cancel());
    }
}
```

**Rules:**
- `[CascadingParameter] private IMudDialogInstance MudDialog` is **required**
- `[Parameter] public TModel Model` receives the model to edit/create
- `Submit()` validates the form, then closes with `DialogResult.Ok(Model)`
- `Cancel()` closes with `DialogResult.Cancel()`
- The model is mutated in-place via `@bind-Value` bindings

