## 3. Confirmation Dialogs (Delete)

For confirmation dialogs (delete, dangerous actions), use `MudMessageBox` with typed `DialogParameters<MudMessageBox>`.

```csharp
private async Task Delete(MyModel model)
{
    var parameters = new DialogParameters<MudMessageBox>
    {
        { x => x.Title, "Delete Item" },
        { x => x.Message, $"Are you sure you want to delete {model.Name}?" },
        { x => x.YesText, "Delete" },
        { x => x.CancelText, "Cancel" }
    };
    var dialog = await _dialog.ShowAsync<MudMessageBox>("", parameters);
    var result = await dialog.Result;
    if (result is { Canceled: false })
    {
        await _store.DeleteAsync(model);
        // refresh UI
    }
}
```

**Rules:**
- Use `DialogParameters<MudMessageBox>` with typed lambda expressions
- Pass an empty string `""` as the title to `ShowAsync` when setting title via parameters
- Check `result.Canceled` before acting

### Real Implementation: OllamaSettings Delete

```csharp
private async Task DeleteAsync(OllamaConnectionInfo model)
