## 4. What NOT to Do (Anti-patterns)

| Anti-pattern | Why it's wrong | Found in |
|-------------|----------------|----------|
| `<MudDialog @bind-Visible="_show">` | This is for inline dialogs, not `IDialogService` dialogs | — |
| `<MudDialog @bind-IsVisible="_show">` | Same — wrong API for service-based dialogs | — |
| `DialogResult.Ok(true)` / `Ok(false)` | Don't return booleans — return the actual model | — |
| `await result.GetReturnValueAsync<bool>()` | Don't extract booleans — check `result.Canceled` | — |
| `new DialogParameters { { "Model", model } }` | Use typed `DialogParameters<T>` with lambdas | `Servers.razor.cs` (Delete only) |
| `new DialogParameters { { nameof(MyDialog.Model), model } }` | Use typed `DialogParameters<T>` with lambdas | — |
| Passing title via `<TitleContent>` in the dialog form | Title goes in `ShowAsync()` first argument | — |
| Using `DialogService` (BootstrapBlazor) or `ResultDialogOption` | These are old APIs, not MudBlazor | Pre-migration code |

**Note on `Servers.razor.cs`:** The `Delete` method in `Servers` uses untyped `DialogParameters` with string keys for `MudMessageBox`. This works but is **not the preferred pattern**. All new code must use `DialogParameters<MudMessageBox>` with typed lambda expressions as shown in `OllamaSettings` and `OpenAISettings`.

---

## 5. Migration from BootstrapBlazor

### What Changed

| BootstrapBlazor | MudBlazor |
|-----------------|-----------|
| `DialogService` | `IDialogService` |
| `ResultDialogOption` | `DialogOptions` |
| `DialogService.ShowAsync<T>(option)` | `IDialogService.ShowAsync<T>(title, parameters, options)` |
| `ToastService` | `ISnackbar` |
| `await _toasts.Error(title, message)` | `_snackbar.Add(message, Severity.Error)` |
| `await _toasts.Success(title, message)` | `_snackbar.Add(message, Severity.Success)` |
| `await _toasts.Warning(title, message)` | `_snackbar.Add(message, Severity.Warning)` |

### Service Registration

MudBlazor services are registered in the application startup (typically in `Cyrena.Shell` or the consuming app):

```csharp
builder.Services.AddMudServices();
```

This registers `IDialogService`, `ISnackbar`, and other MudBlazor services.

---

## 6. Summary of the Pattern

```
Caller Component                          Dialog Form Component
----------------                          ---------------------

1. Creates model                          1. Receives model via [Parameter]
2. Builds DialogParameters<T>             2. Wraps in <MudDialog> (no @bind-Visible)
3. Calls _dialog.ShowAsync<T>(title, ...) 3. Uses <DialogContent> + <DialogActions>
4. Awaits dialog.Result                   4. Validates <MudForm> on Submit
5. Checks result.Canceled                 5. Calls MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Ok(Model))
6. Acts on result                         6. Or MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Cancel())
```

This is the **only correct dialog form pattern** for this solution. Any new dialog form must follow this exactly.

